From: jukeboge <jukeboge@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unisocwifi: support kernels before dev_addr_set()

dev_addr_set() was added in Linux 5.17. OpenWrt 23.05 still uses the
sunxi 5.15 kernel, so fall back to the direct dev_addr assignment there.

Signed-off-by: jukeboge <jukeboge@gmail.com>
---
--- a/unisocwifi/main.c
+++ b/unisocwifi/main.c
@@ -1446,7 +1446,11 @@ static struct sprdwl_vif *sprdwl_register_netdev(struct sprdwl_priv *priv,
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(ndev, wiphy_dev(priv->wiphy));
 
 	sprdwl_set_mac_addr(vif, addr, target_mac_addr);
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 17, 0)
 	dev_addr_set(ndev, target_mac_addr);
+#else
+	memcpy(ndev->dev_addr, target_mac_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+#endif
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_P2P_INTF
 	if (type == NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_DEVICE)
